# Unit Testing — {{project_name}}

<!-- GEN: Why: the agent must see CLI test gates, test-first order, and mandatory rules U1–U14 on one screen so every code change is proven with deterministic unit tests. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

A test proves behavior only if you have seen it fail for the reason it exists. Every unit test must be isolated, deterministic, fast, and verified via CLI.

All CLI test gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`) and review severities (`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`) follow `shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md` and `work-item-contract` (`references/handoff-and-status.md` §9).

---

## 1. CLI Test & Quality Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`)

Every command below is **binary (`exit 0` = `PASS`, `exit != 0` = `FAIL`)**. A skipped, deselected, or uncollected test is `NOT_RUN`, never `PASS`:

| Gate | Command | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **Focused Red / Green Run** | `{{focused_test_cmd}}` | Run one test case to verify red failure reason and green fix (**U12**, **U14**) |
| **Module Unit Suite** | `{{module_test_cmd}}` | Verify all unit tests for the touched module after completing a task |
| **Full Unit Suite** | `{{full_test_cmd}}` | Verify the entire unit test suite at phase end before hand-off |
| **Static Analysis on Tests** | `{{test_lint_cmd}}` | Enforce clean-code formatting, linting, and type checks on test files (**U11**) |

