## 2. When the Test Comes First (Red-to-Green Order)

| Change Type | Order | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| **Domain rules, use cases / services, validation, calculations** | Failing test first | Business logic is where silent wrong results live |
| **Schemas, models, and data mappers** | Failing test first | Missing keys, null rules, or type mismatches break contracts silently |
| **State machines / controllers / routers** | Failing test first | State emission order and error mapping must be proven deterministically |
| **Every bug fix and every review finding fix** | Reproduce with failing test first | A red run on unfixed code is the only proof the defect was real and is now gone |
| **Legacy code lacking tests** | Characterization test first | Locks in existing behavior before modifying code |
| **Pure DI wiring, route registration, or generated code** | May follow | Covered by phase smoke/integration checks (`{{verification_link}}`) |

